      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense i guess, but it still feels super sketchy. like, if the price is just jumping around because of \"supply and demand\" or whatever, how do i know there isn't like, some hidden error or some tiny little things eating away at my money that the app isn't even showing me? is there a way for things to just go wrong in the system without anyone noticing? like tiny little errors or glitches that just live in the background and mess everything up over time?",
      "source": "evaluator"
